See .agent-docs in the relevant directory for documentation of referenced
libraries.

DO NOT START ANY SERVERS. You are in a docker container. STOP AND ASK THE
USER IF YOU NEED A SERVER STARTED TO TEST AGAINST.

We commonly refer to url-base64 (or url-b64). THIS IS NOT STANDARD BASE64
ENCODING. It is "url-safe base64" encoding, and cannot be handled using
standard base64 utils (e.g. tweetnacl-util). You must instead use the
appropriate libraries to work with it (e.g. urlsafe-base64).

WE PRETTY MUCH *NEVER* USE STANDARD base64 ENCODING. STOP AND ASK THE USER IF
YOU THINK IT IS NEEDED.

For rust packages, you can use ./doc-cargo to pull in docs for a crate.
(e.g. `cd tributary-server && ../doc-cargo rand`)
It dumps packages for the library into .agent-docs

The postgres credentials for the test database are in tributary-server/.env

If you're looking for a github project, check the home directory of this
VM. There's a chance it's been fetched already.

You may need my help getting docs for a package you're having issues with.
Pause and let me know if you need help fetching something.

NEVER EVER EVER RUN ANY GIT COMMANDS. YOU ARE BAD AT THEM AND OFTEN DESTROY
